<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  so101_follower - the SO-101 follower arm (TheRobotStudio / Hugging Face
  LeRobot) that rides on the front of the CARMA platform.

  Source. Every joint origin, axis, limit and link mass is copied from the
  official URDF, TheRobotStudio/SO-ARM100 Simulation/SO101/so101_new_calib.urdf
  (Apache-2.0). Each link frame here is the URDF child-link frame, posed
  relative to its parent link by the URDF joint origin, so joint angles mean the
  same thing in both files and a LeRobot recording replays here unchanged.

  Geometry is NOT the URDF's. The URDF draws the printed parts from STL meshes;
  this model draws the five arm links as cylinders from each joint to the next,
  the base as a 110 x 90 x 62.4 mm box, and the gripper as boxes (below). No
  mesh is fetched or vendored, which keeps AGENTS.md section 2.3 (no network at
  run time) trivially true.

  The gripper is NOT the URDF's either. The arm carries a rack-and-pinion
  parallel gripper (GrabCAD "standard open SO-101 arms with parallel gripper"),
  so the URDF's single hinged `gripper` joint is replaced by two prismatic
  fingers, gripper_plus and gripper_minus, that slide in opposite directions.
  Their shape is in gripper_boxes.json, sampled from the project's CAD at 1 to
  3 mm; the two regions of this file marked "generated" are produced from it by
  tools/build_gripper_sdf.py, and tests/test_arm_gripper.py fails if they are
  edited by hand. Provenance, the frame assumptions and an unverified-licence
  caveat are recorded in the JSON and in docs/arm.md. Finger mass is the CAD
  volume times an assumed PLA density; the effort limit is an estimate, not a
  datasheet value.

  Joint limits. Effort is the 12 V STS3215 stall torque, 30 kg.cm = 2.94 N.m;
  velocity is its no-load speed, 0.222 s per 60 deg = 4.7 rad/s. The URDF's own
  effort and velocity entries are placeholders (10 and 10).

  Topics (gz side; bridged by config/bridge.yaml only when the arm is spawned)
    /carma/arm/<joint>/cmd_pos   gz.msgs.Double, target angle in radians, for the
                                 five arm joints
    /carma/arm/gripper_{plus,minus}/cmd_pos   gz.msgs.Double, finger travel in
                                 metres. Not for clients: gripper_relay.py turns
                                 the single /carma/arm/gripper/cmd_pos (radians)
                                 into both
    /carma/arm/joint_states      gz.msgs.Model, the five arm joints and both fingers
    /carma/arm/stereo/{left,right}/image_rgb    gz.msgs.Image, 640 x 480 rgb8, 15 Hz
    /carma/arm/stereo/{left,right}/camera_info  gz.msgs.CameraInfo
  Joints: shoulder_pan, shoulder_lift, elbow_flex, wrist_flex, wrist_roll
  (revolute, radians, the URDF's) and gripper_plus, gripper_minus (prismatic,
  metres, 0 closed to 0.014 open).

  Checked in Gazebo Harmonic (2026-10-23): the arm holds its pose with nothing
  commanded (under 0.002 rad of drift in 3 s); the gripper reaches a command
  within 0.12 s and lands within 0.015 rad of it, the fingers sitting 0.2 mm off
  their targets in opposite directions, which is gravity along the finger axis;
  over-range commands clamp; both cameras stream; the vehicle still drives. The
  fingers' velocity limit is set high on purpose: at 0.1 m/s the joint solver's
  limit chattered against the position controller, pinning the finger velocity
  at the limit and leaving 0.5 to 0.9 mm of hysteresis.

  Grasp frame: gripper_frame, on the roll axis in the distal 20 mm of the
  fingertips, 0.101 m along -z. Reach from the shoulder-lift axis to it is
  0.4135 m, 2.7 mm more than the standard hinged jaw's 0.4108 m.
-->
<sdf version="1.10">
  <model name="so101_follower">

